            "publication_date": "2026-07-09",
            "title": "Harness VLA: Steering Frozen VLAs into Reliable Manipulation Primitives via Memory-Guided Agents",
            "updated_date": "2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295"
          },
          "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W7167900256",
          "title": "Harness VLA: Steering Frozen VLAs into Reliable Manipulation Primitives via Memory-Guided Agents"
        },
        {
          "abstract": "Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models have demonstrated significant potential for generalist robotic policies; however, they struggle to generalize to long-horizon complex tasks in novel real-world domains due to distribution shifts and the scarcity of high-quality demonstrations. Although reinforcement learning (RL) offers a promising avenue for policy improvement, applying it to real-world VLA fine-tuning faces challenges regarding exploration efficiency, training stability, and sample cost. To address these issues, we propose IG-RFT, a novel Interaction-Guided Reinforced Fine-Tuning system designed for flow-based VLA models. Firstly, to facilitate effective policy optimization, we introduce Interaction-Guided Advantage Weighted Regression (IG-AWR), an RL algorithm that dynamically modulates exploration intensity based on the robot’s interaction status. Furthermore, to address the limitations of sparse or task-specific rewards, we design a novel hybrid dense reward function that integrates the trajectory-level reward and the subtask-level reward. Finally, we construct a three-stage RL system comprising SFT, Offline RL, and Human-in-the-Loop RL for fine-tuning VLA models. Extensive real-world experiments on four challenging long-horizon tasks demonstrate that IG-RFT achieves an average success rate of 85.0%, significantly outperforming supervised fine-tuning (SFT) (18.8%) and standard Offline RL baselines (40.0%). Ablation studies confirm the critical contributions of IG-AWR and hybrid reward shaping. In summary, our work establishes and validates a novel reinforced fine-tuning system for VLA models in real-world robotic manipulation. Note to Practitioners—Focusing on the adaptation of general robotic policies to long-horizon complex manipulation scenarios, we develop a reinforcement learning (RL) framework for fine-tuning Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models. Our core innovation is an interaction-guided strategy that balances robustness and exploration to achieve more efficient and effective reinforced fine-tuning (RFT). Furthermore, a hybrid reward function serves as a progress indicator, providing both trajectory guidance and subgoal incentives. All contributions are validated through extensive real-world long-horizon experiments and ablation studies. The proposed methods are applicable to VLA model optimization, providing robust solutions for robotic manipulation in areas such as logistics, service, and warehousing. Building upon this research, future work can explore more large-scale and efficient RL fine-tuning methods for VLA models to further enable generalist policy learning.",
