            "publication_date": "2026-03-24",
            "title": "Gaussian mixtures and non-parametric likelihoods through the lens of statistical mechanics",
            "updated_date": "2026-11-07T11:25:07.637180"
          },
          "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W7140273563",
          "title": "Gaussian mixtures and non-parametric likelihoods through the lens of statistical mechanics"
        },
        {
          "abstract": "We study the nonparametric maximum likelihood estimator (NPMLE) for Gaussian and Poisson mixture models, assuming the support of the true mixing distribution lies in a fixed bounded set. In this setting, we establish exact parametric rates for both, marginal density estimation and the posterior mean when the true mixing distribution is finitely discrete. Moreover, we show that the NPMLE attains the optimal demixing rate previously known for overparameterized finite mixture models. Finally, we identify a new adaptivity phenomenon for inference: the likelihood ratio test statistic is asymptotically tight if and only if the true mixing distribution is finitely discrete.",
          "metadata_retrieval_provenance": {
            "api_version": "public REST API; unversioned endpoint",
