            "publication_date": "2019-09-25",
            "title": "Rademacher complexity for Markov chains: Applications to kernel smoothing and Metropolis–Hastings",
            "updated_date": "2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295"
          },
          "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W2976436354",
          "title": "Rademacher complexity for Markov chains: Applications to kernel smoothing and Metropolis–Hastings"
        },
        {
          "abstract": "This paper is a continuation of work arXiv:2006.09583 devoted to establishment of the convergence rate in the strong invariance principle for cumulative processes. We establish optimal rate of convergence for the case when regeneration periods and increments over them have only power moments of order greater than 2. Under this power-type conditions two types of approximation by Wiener process are proved: the rate of convergence in the Strassen's invariance principle and inequalities for the probability that random process deviates from the approximating one.",
